{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And she conceived.</b> It does not say ותהר, to teach that she was young and pregnancy is not noticeable in her." "<b>And he called his name Gershom.</b> Through the line of justice he should have called his first son after the miracle that HaShem saved him from Pharaoh's sword, yet he did not mention the miracle — only in the name of his younger son, who is Eliezer. One may answer: the salvation was not significant in his eyes as long as the king of Egypt was alive, for he always feared him wherever he went; and when HaShem said to him, 'for all the men who sought your life are dead' — meaning the king of Egypt — then he noted the significance of the miracle. Immediately at that time, when his second son was born to him, as it is written, 'ויהי בדרך במלון' etc., he was punished for not circumcising Eliezer his son who was born at that time. Another interpretation: when Gershom was born, Moses was still new in his place and regarded as a ger, and he was afraid to mention why he had fled from Egypt, lest his father-in-law expel him; but after he had settled, he was no longer concerned."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:54.166841862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}